<p>A Colombian military Lockheed C-130 Hercules crashed shortly after takeoff on Monday near Puerto Leguízamo in the southern department of Putumayo, killing at least 66 people and injuring dozens, according to the armed forces and multiple news outlets. Early official accounts said between 121 and 128 people were on board, mostly soldiers, along with crew members and, in some reports, police personnel. Rescue teams took survivors to hospitals as authorities investigated the cause of the crash. Defence Minister Pedro Sánchez said there was no immediate sign that armed groups had caused it.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JjDvI2NHpZk1jC8-Rd-m9oT443k0ld-tPmCz3z4xbyFK4XAMyRPOV0jvhpj7o_9Saf_oA93bIL6r8GFqYwdVvEWQKEnqwcC9WdnioinhCVIO' alt='A handout photo released by the Colombian Armed Forces shows rescuers lifting injured people on stretchers near Puerto Leguízamo after the crash.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Onboard breakdown: The armed forces chief told reporters the plane was carrying 11 Air Force members, 115 army personnel, and two national police officers.</li><li>Rescue-count swings: Early survivor figures shifted repeatedly. Air Force commander Fernando Silva initially said 48 people had been rescued, and two military sources later told Reuters that 71 had been pulled from the wreckage.</li><li>Flight plan: The aircraft was traveling from La Tagua airstrip in Puerto Leguízamo to Puerto Asís on a routine troop rotation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Defence Minister Pedro Sánchez: Sánchez said the crash appeared to be an accident and that authorities had no immediate evidence linking it to action by armed groups. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8dlmrjn1l2o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>General Carlos Fernando Silva Rueda: The air force commander gave one of the first official breakdowns of those on board, saying the plane carried 110 soldiers and 11 crew members before later casualty totals changed. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-23/colombian-air-force-plane-crashes-with-over-100-soldiers-on-board.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>General Hugo Alejandro López: The head of Colombia’s armed forces later said the confirmed death toll had risen sharply from the earliest official reports and that four military personnel were still missing as the response continued. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/military-plane-with-125-aboard-crashes-in-colombia-at-least-48-rescued/article70777085.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/24/g-s1-114924/at-least-66-killed-in-military-plane-crash-in-colombia-head-of-armed-forces-says'>At least 66 killed in military plane crash in Colombia, head of armed forces says</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/at-least-66-death-in-colombian-military-plane-crash-11257508#publisher=newsstand'>66 Dead In Colombian Military Plane Crash, President Shares Wreckage Video</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/colombia-military-plane-crash/'>Military plane crash in Colombia kills at least 66 people and injures dozens</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s1w2a5/colombian_military_plane_with_125_people_crashes/'>Colombian military plane with 125 people crashes</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-23/colombian-air-force-plane-crashes-with-over-100-soldiers-on-board.html'>Colombian Air Force plane crashes with over 100 soldiers on board</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/23/colombia-military-plane-crash'>At least 66 killed after Colombian military plane crashes in southern Amazon</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3347639/dozens-soldiers-feared-dead-after-colombian-military-plane-crashes-take'>At least 66 dead as Colombia military plane crashes after take-off</a> - scm